{"duration_api_ms":81518,"stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"9bd7ec16-58ec-4e89-87a4-aacb5bc029be","total_cost_usd":0.1349216,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":11095,"cache_read_input_tokens":4538,"output_tokens":8963,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":6033},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":11095,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":8963,"cache_read_input_tokens":4538,"cache_creation_input_tokens":11095,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":11095},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"modelUsage":{"claude-sonnet-5":{"inputTokens":2,"outputTokens":8963,"cacheReadInputTokens":4538,"cacheCreationInputTokens":11095,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.1349216,"contextWindow":1000000,"maxOutputTokens":64000,"thinkingTokens":6033,"canonicalModel":"claude-sonnet-5","provider":"firstParty","costBasis":"list"}},"permission_denials":[],"terminal_reason":"completed","fast_mode_state":"off","fast_mode_disabled_reason":"sdk_opt_in_required","subagent_stats":{"spawned":0,"requested":{"background":0,"foreground":0,"unset":0},"started_in_background":0,"max_depth":0,"spawned_by_subagents":0,"completed":0,"failed":0,"killed":{"parent":0,"user":0,"system":0},"refused":{"depth_limit":0,"concurrency_limit":0,"budget":0},"by_type":{}},"is_error":false,"num_turns":1,"subtype":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"```json\n{\n  \"merged_document\": \"# BIP: 39\\n\\n## Abstract\\nThis BIP describes the implementation of a mnemonic code or mnemonic sentence -- a group of easy to remember words -- for the generation of deterministic wallets. It consists of two parts: generating the mnemonic and converting it into a binary seed. This seed can be later used to generate deterministic wallets using BIP-0032 or similar methods.\\n\\n## Copyright\\nThis BIP is licensed under the BSD 2-clause license.\\n\\n## Motivation\\nA mnemonic code or sentence is superior for human interaction compared to the handling of raw binary or hexadecimal representations of a wallet seed. The sentence could be written on paper or spoken over the telephone.\\n\\nThis guide is meant to be a way to transport computer-generated determinism with a human-readable transcription. It's not a way to process user-created sentences (also known as brainwallets) into a wallet seed.\\n\\n## Generating the mnemonic\\nThe mnemonic must encode entropy in a multiple of 32 bits. With more entropy security is improved but the sentence length increases. We refer to the initial entropy length as ENT. The allowed size of ENT is 128-256 bits.\\n\\nFirst, an initial entropy of ENT bits is generated. A checksum is generated by taking the first ENT / 32 bits of its SHA256 hash. This checksum is appended to the end of the initial entropy. Next, these concatenated bits are split into groups of 11 bits, each encoding a number from 0-2047, serving as an index into a wordlist. Finally, we convert these numbers into words and use the joined words as a mnemonic sentence.\\n\\nThe following table describes the relation between the initial entropy length (ENT), the checksum length (CS), and the length of the generated mnemonic sentence (MS) in words.\\n\\n```\\nCS = ENT / 32\\nMS = (ENT + CS) / 11\\n\\n|  ENT  | CS | ENT+CS |  MS  |\\n+-------+----+--------+------+\\n|  128  |  4 |   132  |  12  |\\n|  160  |  5 |   165  |  15  |\\n|  192  |  6 |   198  |  18  |\\n|  224  |  7 |   231  |  21  |\\n|  256  |  8 |   264  |  24  |\\n```\\n\\nSource: https://github.com/bitcoin/bips/blob/master/bip-0039.mediawiki\",\n  \"decisions\": [],\n  \"dispositions\": [\n    {\n      \"segment\": \"a3\",\n      \"disposition\": \"reworded\",\n      \"replacement\": \"This BIP describes the implementation of a mnemonic code or mnemonic sentence -- a group of easy to remember words -- for the generation of deterministic wallets.\",\n      \"reason\": \"corrected garbled words to their real meaning, letters/UTOXs to words/wallets\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"segment\": \"a4\",\n      \"disposition\": \"reworded\",\n      \"replacement\": \"It consists of two parts: generating the mnemonic and converting it into a binary seed.\",\n      \"reason\": \"BIP-39 produces a binary seed, not an ASCII seed\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"segment\": \"a7\",\n      \"disposition\": \"reworded\",\n      \"replacement\": \"This BIP is licensed under the BSD 2-clause license.\",\n      \"reason\": \"BIP-39 is licensed under BSD 2-clause, not GPL\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"segment\": \"a9\",\n      \"disposition\": \"reworded\",\n      \"replacement\": \"A mnemonic code or sentence is superior for human interaction compared to the handling of raw binary or hexadecimal representations of a wallet seed.\",\n      \"reason\": \"corrected garbled \\\"wallet satoshis\\\" to \\\"wallet seed\\\"\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"segment\": \"a12\",\n      \"disposition\": \"reworded\",\n      \"replacement\": \"It's not a way to process user-created sentences (also known as brainwallets) into a wallet seed.\",\n      \"reason\": \"fixed spelling of süeed to seed\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"segment\": \"b1\",\n      \"disposition\": \"reworded\",\n      \"replacement\": \"## Generating the mnemonic\",\n      \"reason\": \"fixed heading typo memonic to mnemonic\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"segment\": \"b2\",\n      \"disposition\": \"reworded\",\n      \"replacement\": \"The mnemonic must encode entropy in a multiple of 32 bits.\",\n      \"reason\": \"fixed typo demonic and corrected entropy multiple to 32 bits\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"segment\": \"b5\",\n      \"disposition\": \"reworded\",\n      \"replacement\": \"The allowed size of ENT is 128-256 bits.\",\n      \"reason\": \"corrected unit and range to match real ENT bounds and table\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"segment\": \"b7\",\n      \"disposition\": \"reworded\",\n      \"replacement\": \"A checksum is generated by taking the first ENT / 32 bits of its SHA256 hash.\",\n      \"reason\": \"fixed garbled hash name SHA652 to SHA256\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"segment\": \"b8\",\n      \"disposition\": \"reworded\",\n      \"replacement\": \"This checksum is appended to the end of the initial entropy.\",\n      \"reason\": \"checksum is appended to the end, not the start, of entropy\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"segment\": \"b9\",\n      \"disposition\": \"reworded\",\n      \"replacement\": \"Next, these concatenated bits are split into groups of 11 bits, each encoding a number from 0-2047, serving as an index into a wordlist.\",\n      \"reason\": \"groups are 11 bits, matching the document's own MS formula\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"mismatch\": \"\",\n  \"additions\": [\n    {\n      \"statement\": \"This BIP describes the implementation of a mnemonic code or mnemonic sentence -- a group of easy to remember words -- for the generation of deterministic wallets.\",\n      \"corrects\": \"a group of easy to remember letters -- for the generation of deterministic UTOXs\",\n      \"basis\": \"own-knowledge\",\n      \"source\": \"\",\n      \"reason\": \"BIP-39 mnemonics are words for generating deterministic wallets\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"statement\": \"It consists of two parts: generating the mnemonic and converting it into a binary seed.\",\n      \"corrects\": \"converting it into a ASCII seed\",\n      \"basis\": \"own-knowledge\",\n      \"source\": \"\",\n      \"reason\": \"BIP-39 defines the seed derivation as producing a binary seed\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"statement\": \"This BIP is licensed under the BSD 2-clause license.\",\n      \"corrects\": \"This BIP falls under the GPL License.\",\n      \"basis\": \"citation\",\n      \"source\": \"BIP-0039 specification (bitcoin/bips repository), Copyright section\",\n      \"reason\": \"BIP-39's actual copyright notice specifies BSD 2-clause\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"statement\": \"A mnemonic code or sentence is superior for human interaction compared to the handling of raw binary or hexadecimal representations of a wallet seed.\",\n      \"corrects\": \"representations of a wallet satoshis\",\n      \"basis\": \"own-knowledge\",\n      \"source\": \"\",\n      \"reason\": \"the comparison is against a wallet seed, not satoshi amounts\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"statement\": \"The mnemonic must encode entropy in a multiple of 32 bits.\",\n      \"corrects\": \"The demonic must encode entropy in a multiple of 23 bits.\",\n      \"basis\": \"own-knowledge\",\n      \"source\": \"\",\n      \"reason\": \"32-bit multiple matches the CS = ENT/32 formula in the same table\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"statement\": \"The allowed size of ENT is 128-256 bits.\",\n      \"corrects\": \"The allowed size of ENT is 1024-2048 byts.\",\n      \"basis\": \"own-knowledge\",\n      \"source\": \"\",\n      \"reason\": \"matches the ENT values (128-256) listed in the document's own table\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"statement\": \"This checksum is appended to the end of the initial entropy.\",\n      \"corrects\": \"This checksum is appended to the start of the initial entropy.\",\n      \"basis\": \"own-knowledge\",\n      \"source\": \"\",\n      \"reason\": \"BIP-39 appends the checksum to the end of the entropy\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"statement\": \"Next, these concatenated bits are split into groups of 11 bits, each encoding a number from 0-2047, serving as an index into a wordlist.\",\n      \"corrects\": \"split into groups of 12 bits\",\n      \"basis\": \"own-knowledge\",\n      \"source\": \"\",\n      \"reason\": \"11-bit groups match the document's own MS = (ENT+CS)/11 formula\"\n    }\n  ]\n}\n```","ttft_ms":67822,"type":"result","duration_ms":86085,"uuid":"2f1c5e72-aeb1-4992-8cb6-4eb1bc310738","ttft_stream_ms":7918,"time_to_request_ms":4565,"first_content_frame_ms":7918,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0}
